1
00:00:05,175 --> 00:00:07,725
Last time, we put six things in a box.

2
00:00:07,935 --> 00:00:10,785
The robot moved, but it is a non-living thing.

3
00:00:10,985 --> 00:00:14,015
The green bean stayed still, but it is a living thing.

4
00:00:14,225 --> 00:00:15,885
So what are the real clues?

5
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:17,760
Not how it looks.

6
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,250
Not whether it moves.

7
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:20,650
Ask two things.

8
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:21,880
What does it need?

9
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:23,220
What can it do?

10
00:00:23,719 --> 00:00:26,299
Living things need water, food and air.

11
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:29,949
Living things grow, respond to changes and reproduce.

12
00:00:30,189 --> 00:00:32,629
You will test these in the next two episodes.

13
00:00:33,645 --> 00:00:34,712
Say it with us!

14
00:00:35,372 --> 00:00:36,772
Does it move?

15
00:00:38,672 --> 00:00:40,072
That's NOT the clue!

16
00:00:41,972 --> 00:00:43,372
What does it NEED?

17
00:00:45,272 --> 00:00:46,672
What can it DO?

18
00:00:48,572 --> 00:00:49,972
Does it move?

19
00:00:50,222 --> 00:00:51,622
That's NOT the clue!

20
00:00:51,872 --> 00:00:53,272
What does it NEED?

21
00:00:53,522 --> 00:00:54,922
What can it DO?

22
00:00:56,452 --> 00:00:57,332
Day ten.

23
00:00:57,552 --> 00:01:01,792
Time to sort all six into two groups: living things and non-living

24
00:01:01,542 --> 00:01:02,232
things.

25
00:01:02,452 --> 00:01:03,922
Momo, you go first.

26
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:05,290
Squish...

27
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:06,310
squish...

28
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:07,720
knock, knock.

29
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:08,620
Done!

30
00:01:09,054 --> 00:01:10,524
Something is not right.

31
00:01:10,734 --> 00:01:12,834
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

32
00:01:13,054 --> 00:01:13,964
Hold on!

33
00:01:19,471 --> 00:01:20,581
Arms crossed?

34
00:01:20,801 --> 00:01:21,921
One finger up!

35
00:01:22,161 --> 00:01:22,831
Look.

36
00:01:23,081 --> 00:01:25,251
The teddy bear is sitting with the mealworm.

37
00:01:25,491 --> 00:01:27,521
Momo sorted by soft and hard.

38
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,380
I wanted to know how they feel!

39
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:30,470
Good sort.

40
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:31,830
Wrong question.

41
00:01:32,410 --> 00:01:34,430
Momo did put things into groups.

42
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:36,050
Alike things together.

43
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:37,800
Different things apart.

44
00:01:38,304 --> 00:01:39,504
Say it with me!

45
00:01:40,217 --> 00:01:45,137
Classification is the grouping of things based on their similarities and differences.

46
00:01:47,062 --> 00:01:50,662
Similarities: characteristics that things have in common.

47
00:01:54,137 --> 00:01:55,927
You can choose soft or hard.

48
00:01:56,137 --> 00:01:58,677
But our question is living or non-living.

49
00:01:58,897 --> 00:02:00,567
So we use the real clues.

50
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:02,267
Has anyone done that?

51
00:02:04,039 --> 00:02:05,729
My homework from Day one.

52
00:02:05,929 --> 00:02:08,319
I fixed the green bean after Round two.

53
00:02:08,442 --> 00:02:09,322
Showdown!

54
00:02:09,562 --> 00:02:10,652
Double points.

55
00:02:10,862 --> 00:02:12,922
Pip made a table with two columns.

56
00:02:13,142 --> 00:02:15,222
One thing is still in the wrong column.

57
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:19,900
Is it one, the wind-up robot?

58
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:21,200
Two, the plant?

59
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:22,680
Or three, the pebble?

60
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,320
Show me with your fingers.

61
00:02:30,792 --> 00:02:31,742
Locked in!

62
00:02:31,872 --> 00:02:32,512
Two!

63
00:02:32,632 --> 00:02:33,882
We water that plant.

64
00:02:33,922 --> 00:02:35,022
It needs water.

65
00:02:35,075 --> 00:02:35,865
Two!

66
00:02:35,925 --> 00:02:37,295
I saw a new leaf.

67
00:02:37,346 --> 00:02:39,376
But it never moved out of its pot!

68
00:02:39,953 --> 00:02:42,663
Watch the plant, from day one to day fourteen.

69
00:02:42,903 --> 00:02:44,323
It stays in its pot.

70
00:02:44,523 --> 00:02:45,883
But it has a new leaf.

71
00:02:46,093 --> 00:02:48,343
And it grows towards the light from the window.

72
00:02:48,553 --> 00:02:50,323
The plant is a living thing.

73
00:02:51,664 --> 00:02:52,334
Fixed!

74
00:02:52,084 --> 00:02:54,644
A plant stays in one place.

75
00:02:54,794 --> 00:02:56,544
But it is a living thing.

76
00:02:56,666 --> 00:02:57,656
Two fingers?

77
00:02:57,876 --> 00:02:59,756
Put up two more on your score hand!

78
00:03:00,329 --> 00:03:01,699
Pip used a table.

79
00:03:01,899 --> 00:03:04,629
The same two groups can be shown in other ways too.

80
00:03:04,825 --> 00:03:05,925
Say it with me!

81
00:03:06,638 --> 00:03:11,368
We can present our classification using pictures, a table, and a graphic

82
00:03:11,118 --> 00:03:12,088
organiser.

83
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:18,660
Day thirty.

84
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:20,230
What is under the cloth?

85
00:03:22,545 --> 00:03:24,705
The green bean is a tall plant now.

86
00:03:24,915 --> 00:03:26,315
The mealworm is bigger.

87
00:03:26,535 --> 00:03:28,125
The plant has new leaves.

88
00:03:28,355 --> 00:03:30,795
And the teddy bear, the robot and the pebble?

89
00:03:31,035 --> 00:03:32,375
Exactly the same.

90
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:34,441
Three living things.

91
00:03:34,651 --> 00:03:36,121
Three non-living things.

92
00:03:36,771 --> 00:03:37,838
Say it with us!

93
00:03:38,498 --> 00:03:39,898
Does it move?

94
00:03:41,798 --> 00:03:43,198
That's NOT the clue!

95
00:03:45,098 --> 00:03:46,498
What does it NEED?

96
00:03:48,398 --> 00:03:49,798
What can it DO?

97
00:03:51,698 --> 00:03:53,098
Does it move?

98
00:03:53,348 --> 00:03:54,748
That's NOT the clue!

99
00:03:54,998 --> 00:03:56,398
What does it NEED?

100
00:03:56,648 --> 00:03:58,048
What can it DO?

101
00:03:59,253 --> 00:04:00,643
Show me your score hand!

102
00:04:00,873 --> 00:04:01,883
More than two?

103
00:04:02,113 --> 00:04:03,393
You beat the Buddies.

104
00:04:03,613 --> 00:04:04,673
Three fingers?

105
00:04:04,893 --> 00:04:05,893
High five!

106
00:04:06,390 --> 00:04:07,750
Did you spot the lizard?

107
00:04:07,990 --> 00:04:10,330
It was on the window frame on day fourteen.

108
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:12,640
Is a lizard living or non-living?

109
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:14,130
Tell someone at home.

110
00:04:15,793 --> 00:04:16,603
Oh no.

111
00:04:16,783 --> 00:04:17,873
Is it sad?

112
00:04:18,003 --> 00:04:19,713
A drooping plant isn't sad.

113
00:04:19,933 --> 00:04:20,953
What does it need?

114
00:04:21,213 --> 00:04:23,103
Lock in your answer for next time.

115
00:04:24,135 --> 00:04:26,295
Let's read today's key words together!

116
00:04:26,535 --> 00:04:27,255
Ready?

117
00:04:27,595 --> 00:04:28,624
Classification.

118
00:04:28,822 --> 00:04:30,131
Classification.

119
00:04:30,681 --> 00:04:31,391
Table.

120
00:04:31,445 --> 00:04:32,280
Table.

121
00:04:32,831 --> 00:04:34,281
Graphic organiser.

122
00:04:34,287 --> 00:04:35,737
Graphic organiser.

123
00:04:36,287 --> 00:04:37,187
Well done!

124
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:39,231
Say it with us!

125
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:40,740
Ready?

126
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:41,810
One, two...

127
00:04:41,949 --> 00:04:42,859
Now you know!

128
